flowchart TB
  accTitle: Different objects selected by modern and historical workspace baselines
  accDescr: LIDA competition selects a codelet coalition and GWA provides a bounded working stage with attention selection and broadcast. DyLAN selects an agent team. Adaptive graph pruning selects agent nodes and communication edges. Hearsay-II schedules knowledge sources over shared partial hypotheses. Top-k retrieval selects individual items. These mechanisms should not be treated as selecting the same object.
  subgraph W[Content and workspace]
    L[LIDA] --> LC[Codelet coalition]
    G[GWA] --> GC[Working content and broadcast]
  end
  subgraph A[Agent collaboration]
    D[DyLAN] --> DT[Agent team]
    P[Adaptive graph pruning] --> PG[Agent nodes and edges]
  end
  subgraph S[Other shared-context mechanisms]
    H[Hearsay-II] --> HP[Partial hypotheses and enabled sources]
    T[Top-k retrieval] --> TI[Individual retrieved items]
  end
  LC --> GAP[Distinct candidate objects; B3 targets typed content coalitions]
  GC --> GAP
  DT --> GAP
  PG --> GAP
  HP --> GAP
  TI --> GAP
  classDef source fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef process fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef output fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef caution fill:#FEF9E7,stroke:#F39C12,color:#1C1C1E
  class L,G,D,P,H,T source
  class LC,GC,DT,PG,HP,TI process
  class GAP caution
